# 4. Behavior Summary

| Interaction | Result |
| :--- | :--- |
| Drag a column by its grip handle | Reorders columns → persisted via `reorderSprintColumns` |
| Kebab menu → **Edit column** | Opens editor (title + status); status disabled if already used |
| Kebab menu → **Delete column** | Confirm modal → `removeSprintColumn` (tasks kept) |
| Toolbar → **Add column** | Editor with the first unused status preselected |
| Drag a task between columns | `moveSprintStatus` → writes `chat.status` |
| **New Task** (toolbar/column) | Created with the column's status via `newSprintTask` |
| New sprint created | Seeded with default columns (`createSprintBoard`) |

### Notes / Follow-ups
- **Wiring**: `SprintBoardView.vue` still needs to be mounted for sprint-type boards (e.g., conditionally in `KanbanContainer.vue`/`Kanban.vue` when `$storex.kanban.isSprintBoard`). That was intentionally left out to keep this change focused.
- **Backend**: sprint columns are stored as generic JSON on the board via the existing `/api/kanban` save; no API change required. Column `status` values stay within the canonical `CHAT_STATUS_CONFIG` set so status badges/icons remain consistent.

